  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"A collaborative project of collected stories, rumors, little known facts or folktales about artists and designers."--Box inner lid.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Project based on exhibition: Van Gogh's ear and other art stories.  Cf. information leaf.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Contributors: Robert Brinkerhoff, Memphis, Tennessee, Harvey Kaner, Los Angeles, California, Jim Walker, Chicago, Illinois, Jacob Livshultz, New York, New York, Maria Rougal, Richmond, Virginia, Alexsandra Sukhoy, Chicago, Illinois. Book Arts Grant: Women's Studio Workshop.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"Supported in part with public funds from the Women's Studio Workshop and the New York State Council on the Arts."--Box.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Designed so that the reader/viewer interacts with text that has been communicated through "word of mouth", in a symbolic way of "hanging out the dirty laundry." Cf. information leaf.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Contains twelve "sheets" of unbleached muslin (12 x 8 cm), with text printed in black; 12 wooden spring clothes pins; 1 piece of string (148 cm). Objects, along with information leaf, rest within a brown cardboard box.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Issued in a limited edition of 125 numbered copies.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">LC has copy number 56.</subfield>
